// Go workspace for this repository.
//
// Modules, and they are not peers:
//
//	sync/         the generator: specification in, protobuf out.
//	codec/        converts between the schema and the VSS shape. A consumer
//	              of the model, never a part of producing it.
//	sandbox/go/   a go.mod *template*, copied over gen/go in CI so the
//	              generated protobuf Go can be compiled. It holds no
//	              packages of its own.
//
// The first two are workspace members, which is what lets codec import sync
// without either being published: the `replace` in codec/go.mod names the
// path, and the workspace resolves it against this checkout.
//
// The template is deliberately left out: adding it would put a module in the
// workspace that has nothing to build, and the tree it describes -- gen/go --
// does not exist until `buf generate` has run.
//
// That omission has a consequence worth knowing. Once a go.work exists at the
// repository root, a `go build` run *inside* gen/go resolves this workspace
// and fails, because gen/go is not a member. CI and the justfile therefore
// set GOWORK=off for that build; see .github/workflows/generate.yml.
go 1.24

use (
	./sync
	./codec
)
